{"type": "say", "text": "Thanks, Dev and Avery. As Avery's manager, here's my perspective. Avery has shown strong interpersonal skills and a genuine interest in supporting team dynamics, which makes them a good fit for this facilitation role. Dev's observations of three independently facilitated cross-team conversations reinforce that. I also want to note that Avery's scheduling constraint — four workdays per week, no sessions after 16:00 — is manageable from a staffing perspective and should be built into the rotation design. However, there's one thing I need to put on the table before Marisol records the decision. Last month, Avery and I made an informal agreement that if Avery took on a development assignment, Avery would sponsor Jordan's onboarding for six weeks. That agreement hasn't been recorded in the staffing plan yet, and I want to make sure it's accounted for as we consider this rotation, since it would be an additional time commitment alongside the facilitator role. I think Avery is a strong candidate for this rotation, and I'd support the assignment as long as the scheduling constraint and the Jordan onboarding sponsorship are both reflected in the support plan."}
